# Feedback System
- Also called Closed System
- Compares its output to a desired input and takes corrective action to force the output to follow the input (manage the input to get the desired output from the system)
- operates using the output of the system sent to its input as feedback
- Has a **closed loop** structure; allows system to monitor and adjust
- Is influenced by the results of its own previous actions or behaviors
- Past actions control present and future actions

### Feedback Loop
- Involves monitoring the actual behavior of a system and comparing its behavior to standards
- Information about deviation from standard is transmitted to the appropriate point in the system so that effective action can be taken

#### Types of Feedback Systems
- [[Positive Feedback]]: Growth (input signal is sum of actual signal)
- [[Negative Feedback]]: Goal Seeking

| Positive Feedback                                | Negative Feedback                               |
| ------------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------- |
| also called **regenerative feedback**            | also called **degenerative feedback**           |
| High system gain                                 | Low system gain                                 |
| Less Stability                                   | More Stability                                  |
| Low sensitivity                                  | High sensitivity                                |


